# .gitignore — TourSearch
#
# Policy source: docs/architecture.md ("Configuration and secrets"),
#                docs/scraping.md ("Snapshots"), docs/conventions.md.
# Everything below is a rule for artifacts that DO NOT belong in git.
# docs/ and README.md must stay tracked — the negations for them are at the
# END of this file, because gitignore is last-match-wins and an earlier
# negation can be re-ignored by any later pattern.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- docs ------
# Specification files are never ignored. See the !docs/** rules at the bottom.

# ------------------------------------------------------------- secrets ------
# Credentials never come from a committed file. Local dev uses User Secrets,
# which generates a *.LocalSecrets.env next to the project.
*.LocalSecrets.env
**/*.LocalSecrets.env
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/*.local.json
# Narrow on purpose: this repo runs with core.ignorecase = true, so **/secrets*
# would also ignore a real source file named Secrets.cs. List the shapes instead.
**/secrets
**/secrets.json
**/secrets.env
**/secrets.toml
**/secrets.yaml
**/secrets.yml
**/.secrets
**/.secrets.*

# Generic dotenv-style files: only *.example is allowed in the repo.
.env
.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/*.env.example

# Private keys / certs — uncomment only if you are sure no legit *.pem/*.crt
# file must ever be tracked in this repo.
# *.pem
# *.crt
# *.p12
# *.key

# --------------------------------------------------------- scraped data -----
# HTML snapshots of TourVisor.ru: third-party content, unbounded, TTL-managed.
# They live outside the repo (TOURSEARCH_SNAPSHOT_DIR); this is a safety net.
**/snapshots/**

# Scratch helpers written while auditing these docs (e.g. .tmp-anchor-check.js).
.tmp-*
tmp-*

# ------------------------------------------------------- Playwright (.NET) --
# playwright.ps1 (the launcher) IS tracked; the downloaded browser binaries
# are not. Default cache is ~/.cache/ms-playwright; with PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH
# unset they also land next to the app under ms-playwright/.
**/playwright/**
!**/playwright.ps1
**/.cache/ms-playwright/**
**/ms-playwright/**
# Deliberately NO bare **/chromium-*/ pattern: it matches tests/fixtures/chromium-10/,
# and a file inside an excluded directory cannot be re-included by a later negation,
# so **/fixtures/** could not rescue it. Fixture dirs are kept by not matching them at all.

# ------------------------------------------------------------- build --------
# .NET 10 build cache and generic output dirs.
.build/
build/
dist/
out/
target/
**/obj/

# Compiled artifacts (defensive: these should never be committed anyway).
*.dll
*.exe
*.o
*.obj
*.so
*.a
*.lib
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.met
*.pac
*.dSYM
*.dSYM.zip

# ------------------------------------------------------------- tests --------
# Test output, coverage, reporters. Testcontainers generate their own temp dirs.
**/coverage/**
*.coverage
*.coverage.*
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info
**/TestResults/**
**/htmloutput/**
# Anchored: a bare **/report/** would ignore docs/report/x.md, which is a spec file.
/report/**
*.lcov

# ------------------------------------------------------------- runtime -------
# Logs, profiling dumps, temp files.
**/logs/**
*.log
*.heapsnapshot
*.cpuprofile
*.trace
*.trace.json.gz
*.tmp
*.temp
# Anchored: a bare **/tmp/** would ignore src/**/Tmp/** source files, which are
# legitimate on a case-insensitive filesystem.
/tmp/**
*.bak
*.swp
*.swo
*~
#*#
*.orig
*.rej

# --------------------------------------------------------- tooling / OS -----
.idea/
*.iml
.fleet/
.vscode/
# If you keep shared editor settings in the repo, un-ignore them:
# !.vscode/
*.sublime-workspace
*.code-workspace
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
[Dd]esktop.ini
node_modules/

# ------------------------------------------------------------- DB / local ---
# Local PostgreSQL data dirs if someone runs psql inside the repo.
**/pgs/**
**/postgres_data/**
**/data/sql/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- docs ------
# LAST MATCH WINS — these negations must come after every ignore rule above so
# that no later pattern can re-ignore the specification.
!docs/**
!README.md
!AGENTS.md
